<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaaba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ka'bah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaaba is a cube-shaped building at the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjid-al-haram">Great Mosque of Mecca</a>, the holiest site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Before Islam it was a shrine housing many idols, visited by pilgrims from across western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. After taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 630 Muhammad cleared away the idols, and Muslims worldwide face the Kaaba in prayer and circle it during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajj">hajj</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaaba.jpg" alt="Kaaba" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Mortel · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Ka%27ba,_Great_Mosque_of_Mecca,_Saudi_Arabia_(4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
